# Accessibility Guidelines

## ARIA Guidelines

- Use proper ARIA labels
- Implement keyboard navigation
- Ensure proper focus management
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide alternative text for images

## Color and Contrast

- Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
- Support dark/light themes
- Test with screen readers
- Use sufficient color contrast ratios
- Don't rely solely on color to convey information

## Keyboard Navigation

- Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- Implement proper tab order
- Use skip links for navigation
- Provide keyboard shortcuts for common actions
- Handle focus in modals and overlays

## Screen Reader Support

- Use proper heading hierarchy (h1-h6)
- Provide alternative text for images
- Use descriptive link text
- Implement proper form labels
- Use ARIA landmarks

## Focus Management

- Maintain logical focus order
- Provide visible focus indicators
- Handle focus in modals and overlays
- Return focus when closing modals
- Use focus traps when necessary

## Semantic HTML

```typescript
// Good - semantic HTML
<main>
  <h1>Events</h1>
  <section aria-labelledby="events-heading">
    <h2 id="events-heading">My Events</h2>
    <article>
      <h3>Event Title</h3>
      <p>Event content...</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</main>

// Bad - non-semantic
<div>
  <div>Events</div>
  <div>
    <div>My Events</div>
    <div>
      <div>Event Title</div>
      <div>Event content...</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Interactive Elements

```typescript
// Accessible button
<button
  onClick={handleClick}
  onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
  aria-label="Delete event"
  aria-describedby="delete-description"
>
  <TrashIcon aria-hidden="true" />
  <span>Delete</span>
</button>
<div id="delete-description" className="sr-only">
  Permanently delete this event
</div>

// Screen reader only class
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}
```

## Skip Links

```typescript
// Skip to main content link
<a href="#main-content" className="skip-link">
  Skip to main content
</a>

<main id="main-content" tabIndex={-1}>
  {/* Main content */}
</main>

// CSS for skip link
.skip-link {
  position: absolute;
  top: -40px;
  left: 6px;
  background: #000;
  color: #fff;
  padding: 8px;
  text-decoration: none;
  z-index: 1000;
}

.skip-link:focus {
  top: 6px;
}
```

## Testing Accessibility

- Use axe-core for automated testing
- Test with screen readers (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver)
- Test keyboard navigation
- Test with high contrast mode
- Test with zoom (200% and 400%)

## Accessibility Checklist

- [ ] Semantic HTML structure
- [ ] Proper heading hierarchy
- [ ] Alternative text for images
- [ ] Keyboard navigation
- [ ] Focus management
- [ ] Color contrast compliance
- [ ] Screen reader compatibility
- [ ] Form accessibility
- [ ] Modal accessibility
- [ ] Skip links
- [ ] ARIA labels and descriptions
- [ ] Error message accessibility
- [ ] Loading state accessibility
